<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar output reaches 5.35 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar output reaches 5.35 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai sugar output for the crushing season which started in November reached 5.35 million tonnes compared with 5.29 million during the same period last year, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The yield, which also improved over the week, still tracked that of the previous crushing season, they said.</p>
<p>As of March 26, a total of 52.07 million tonnes of sugar cane had been crushed to produce 3.07 million tonnes of raw sugar and 2.28 million tonnes of white.</p>
<p>The following is the comparison of this season's sugar cane crushing details with the same period last season (in tonnes unless otherwise specified):</p>
<p>					March 26, 1997    March 26, 1996</p>
<p>Crushed sugar cane		 52,070,266	   50,134,022</p>
<p>Raw Sugar			     3,065,885	    3,057,980</p>
<p>White and refined sugar	   2,282,983	    2,236,251</p>
<p>Commercial Cane Sugar (pct)	11.63		     12.07</p>
<p>Yield				   102.72		    105.60</p>
<p>Mollasses			     2,263,636	     2,341,507</p>
<p>Yield				    43.47		     46.70</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
